.TH DASL 1 "2026-10-12" "ASL 1.42.313" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dasl \- disassemble binary or Intel HEX images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dasl
\-cpu name \-binfile file [options]
.br
.B dasl
\-cpu name \-hexfile file [options]
.br
.B dasl \-help
.br
.B dasl \-version
.br
.B dasl \-cpu list
.SH DESCRIPTION
Load input with an explicit \-binfile or \-hexfile option. Bare positional
filenames do not load an image. Available decoder CPUs are listed by
\-cpu list; they are a subset of the assembler's targets. Assembly text
is written to stdout. Quote paths and arguments containing shell metacharacters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-cpu name
Select the decoder, or use list (or ?) to list decoders and exit.
.TP
.B \-binfile file[@start[,length[,granularity]]]
Load a binary image with optional address, length and address granularity.
.TP
.B \-hexfile file
Load an Intel HEX image.
.TP
.B \-entryaddress address,name
Define a direct entry point and label.
.TP
.B \-entryaddress (address[,length[,MSB|LSB]]),name
Read an indirect entry point from the image using the specified byte order.
.TP
.B \-symbol address=name
Define a label at an address.
.TP
.B \-h
Use lowercase hexadecimal output.
.TP
.B \-screenheight lines
Enable help/CPU-list paging; zero disables paging.
.TP
.B \-help, \-version
Print help or version information and exit successfully.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
DASCMD presets options before the command line. Key files use @filename
and shared command-line parsing; options and arguments stay on the same line.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Message catalogs are embedded by default. External-catalog builds use
AS_MSGPATH for one catalog directory. LC_MESSAGES, LC_ALL and LANG select
catalog language, in that order.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asl (1)
